erbocker ahead is a DCCC internal; July surveys had Turner up seven", "A favorable midterm environment and solid challenger fundraising keep the race competitive"], "rationale": "Turner's incumbency and the district's Republican lean outweigh a favorable midterm climate for Democrats; the only poll showing Knickerbocker ahead is a Democratic committee internal, while most raters call the race Likely Republican and markets price her win chance near one in four.", "watch": "Independent polling confirming the October Democratic internal that showed Knickerbocker narrowly ahead would push this toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Turner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Mike Turner seeks another term in the Dayton-area district, which leans Republican by about four points. He has out-raised Democrat Kristina Knickerbocker and holds a cash advantage, and most election analysts rate the contest as likely or solidly Republican. Prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-four chance of winning.\n\nKnickerbocker has run a well-funded campaign in what appears to be a favorable midterm climate for her party, and a Democratic committee's October poll showed her narrowly ahead after July surveys had Turner up seven points. That gap between the internal polling and the expert consensus adds uncertainty, but the incumbent's track record and the district's lean make him the clear favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1787, "margin": -5.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1387, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1203, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.119, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1452, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1169, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1457, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_d